{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start the process for ACME, begin with the New Resupply Cycle and then Check Levels of Inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening span establishes the process trigger (init), followed directly by the two sequential actions n1 and n2. All three elements faithfully capture the starting phase."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4",
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the inventory is below or equal to the minimum, generate an Equal to or below minimum Report. If the inventory is greater than the minimum, generate an Above Minimum Report."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional introduces an XOR branch (b1) and an explicit check action (n3). The guards correctly abstract the thresholds ('below_or_equal' and 'above'), and actions n4/n5 match the corresponding report generation steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the report indicates that the inventory is equal to or below the minimum, create Purchase Orders (POs)."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n7 directly implements the PO creation step described in this unit."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the report indicates that the inventory is above the minimum, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n6 models the early termination condition, while e1 represents the structural end node signaled by the text."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9",
        "guard:b2->n11",
        "action:n11",
        "guard:b2->n10",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the PO is rejected, it needs to be reworked. If the PO is approved, it is printed and released in the system."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional approval/rejection logic is captured by branch b2 and check action n9. Guards correctly route to rejection (n11 rework) and approval (n10 print/release) paths, matching the source exactly."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n8 faithfully implements the PO review step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, reserve funds for the released POs and mail the POs to the supplier."
      ],
      "justification": "The temporal marker 'Simultaneously' justifies the AND branch b3, which splits into the two parallel actions n12 and n13. All elements align with the source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If funds are reserved for the released POs, receive the Packing Slip. If the POs are mailed to the supplier, receive the inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Actions n14 and n15 correspond directly to the two receipt steps triggered by the parallel tasks."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the Packing Slip is received, proceed to receive the Invoice. If the inventory is received, proceed to receive the Packing Slip."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n16 captures the invoice receipt step. The second clause reiterates packing slip receipt, which is already covered by n14, so no additional element is required."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n17",
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the Invoice is received, proceed to the Three-way match."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n17 covers proceeding to the match, and n18 covers performing it. The slight elaboration is semantically equivalent and falls under acceptable redundancy."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the Three-way match is successful, release the funds."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n19 accurately reflects the conditional fund release upon successful matching."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the funds are released, issue the payment."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n20 directly matches the payment issuance step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n21"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the payment is issued, the Resupply Cycle is complete and the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Action n21 and end node e2 jointly capture the cycle completion and process termination described in the closing sentence."
    }
  ],
